## Gate 5: precise handoff

Completed here: source implementation and Source-CI verification of a bounded,
one-shot created-OCI identity handoff, plus protection against unintended old
workflow repeats. Live Docker compatibility of this new verifier has not yet
been exercised. Full guardian/rootfs/worker composition is still unfinished.

Next: use the accepted software in a bounded real guardian composition, with
safe export/extraction provenance, a read-only rootfs bootstrap that does not
substitute host runtime files, and explicit delivery of the accepted software
identity into worker admission/controller agreement. Verify that actual workload
processes, not merely a Docker CLI, are contained before release. Exercise that
composition's positive and negative paths together; do not count synthetic
metadata tests as native proof or repeat the old build to manufacture progress.

The existing real-worker entry remains closed. Dedicated host/S3/data binding,
approved H100/CUDA testing and actual SFT remain downstream. No GPU/instance,
S3/SSH, real model/data, training, registry mutation, dataset seal or production
promotion occurred. The Mac ran only lightweight source/synthetic/AST tests and
metadata/publication commands. This result-only receipt is not pushed, avoiding
another Source/Spark run solely for documentation.
